  "semantics": "Optional nonoverlapping expansion macros with retained graphic-unit costs. Abstract expansion-labelled paths reversible, but ambiguous physical marks require extra cipher disambiguation. Not an encoder/codebook or complete historical abbreviation system.",
  "limitations": [
    "Frozen before new capacity scoring, not optimized from Voynich substrings.",
    "Combines conventions from different periods; compatibility does not demonstrate common historical use.",
    "Marked letters treated as compound units while separate retained letters/signs are counted; EVA-unit comparability uncertain.",
    "Nasal profiles are disambiguated capacity envelopes, not validated uniquely decodable historic mark systems.",
    "One-unit-macro profile intentionally optimistic and not a paleographic count.",
    "Rule coverage need not be exhaustive; stop after fixed profiles."
  ]
